  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready at `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key at `keys/0002.json`. It's titled \"Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow\" and has six questions on O4:\n\n- **Questions:** three multiple-choice, one numeric and two short-answer.\n- **Topics:**\n  - q1 asks what separates a workflow from an agent.\n  - q2 asks you to classify a routing design.\n  - q3 asks which design suits the booking steps.\n  - q4 is a cost comparison in model calls.\n  - q5 asks you to classify a design where the model only picks among branches fixed in advance.\n  - q6 asks when a fixed workflow is the better choice.\n- **Mission link:** the questions use the makerspace assistant and your small model budget.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** there is no lesson on O4 yet. I wrote the quiz from the objective's wording and from what I already know about workflows and agents, and I didn't search for or read a source. The definitions are the standard ones from Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\", but I haven't re-checked them against it. I can write a lesson next if you want one.\n- **New misconception ids:** the key uses M7 to M9. M7 is that using tools or several model calls makes something an agent. M8 is that an agent is always the more capable choice. M9 is that the difference is about how many tools a system has.\n\nI haven't shown any answers.",
